WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.206
School and Parent-Teacher Meeting.

2
00:00:02.486 --> 00:00:06.881
Day 55 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.631 --> 00:00:09.655
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.935 --> 00:00:19.129
Today's goal: talk to schools about admissions, discuss your child's progress with teachers, raise concerns respectfully, and agree on how to help at home.

5
00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:21.333
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.613 --> 00:00:22.573
Key words.

7
00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.167
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:25.447 --> 00:00:35.367
Word or phrase, and Meaning. admission or entrance test or interview: joining a school. class teacher or subject teacher or principal: school staff.

9
00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:59.135
PTM (parent-teacher meeting): regular progress meeting. report card or marks or grades or assessment: results. homework or project or assignment: work at home. behaviour or attention or participation: how the child acts in class. extracurricular activities: sports, music, clubs. fee structure or transport or uniform: admin topics.

10
00:01:00.485 --> 00:01:01.359
Part 2.

11
00:01:01.639 --> 00:01:02.855
Questions you'll ask.

12
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:05.087
Admissions.

13
00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.628
What is the admission process for Class 3?

14
00:01:07.908 --> 00:01:11.428
Which board do you follow (CBSE or ICSE or IB)?

15
00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:14.801
What's the class size? / student, teacher ratio?

16
00:01:15.081 --> 00:01:16.425
What's the fee structure?

17
00:01:16.705 --> 00:01:18.220
Are there any other charges?

18
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.484
Is there school transport from our area?

19
00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:22.837
PTM.

20
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:25.079
How is she doing in class overall?

21
00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:27.429
Which subjects does he find difficult?

22
00:01:27.709 --> 00:01:29.821
How is his behaviour with other children?

23
00:01:30.101 --> 00:01:31.594
What can we do at home to help?

24
00:01:31.874 --> 00:01:33.538
Is she participating in class?

25
00:01:33.818 --> 00:01:36.229
How can I contact you if I have a concern?

26
00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:38.475
Part 3.

27
00:01:38.755 --> 00:01:41.229
Conversation 1: parent-teacher meeting.

28
00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:44.506
Here is how the conversation goes.

29
00:01:44.786 --> 00:01:46.087
Good morning, Mr.

30
00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.071
Gupta.

31
00:01:47.351 --> 00:01:48.631
Please sit down.

32
00:01:48.911 --> 00:01:50.170
Good morning, ma'am.

33
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.389
Thank you.

34
00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:53.866
How is Aarav doing this term?

35
00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:56.258
He's doing well in maths and science.

36
00:01:56.538 --> 00:01:57.861
He's very curious.

37
00:01:58.141 --> 00:01:59.314
That's good to hear.

38
00:01:59.594 --> 00:02:00.959
What about English?

39
00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:03.799
His reading is good, but his writing needs work.

40
00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:07.023
He makes spelling mistakes and doesn't finish his sentences.

41
00:02:08.373 --> 00:02:09.973
The conversation continues.

42
00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:11.192
I see.

43
00:02:11.472 --> 00:02:13.328
What can we do at home to help?

44
00:02:13.608 --> 00:02:17.213
Ask him to write a short diary every day, five or six lines.

45
00:02:17.493 --> 00:02:19.413
And read together for 15 minutes.

46
00:02:19.693 --> 00:02:20.995
We can do that.

47
00:02:21.275 --> 00:02:23.152
How is his behaviour in class?

48
00:02:23.432 --> 00:02:26.227
He's friendly, but sometimes he talks during lessons.

49
00:02:27.577 --> 00:02:29.177
The conversation continues.

50
00:02:29.457 --> 00:02:31.419
I'll speak to him about that.

51
00:02:31.699 --> 00:02:34.110
Could we check his progress again in a month?

52
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.307
Of course.

53
00:02:35.587 --> 00:02:37.273
You can email me any time.

54
00:02:37.553 --> 00:02:39.857
Thank you so much for your time, ma'am.

55
00:02:41.207 --> 00:02:42.124
Part 4.

56
00:02:42.404 --> 00:02:44.857
Conversation 2: raising a concern.

57
00:02:46.107 --> 00:02:48.134
Here is how the conversation goes.

58
00:02:48.414 --> 00:02:51.529
Ma'am, I'd like to discuss something that's worrying us.

59
00:02:51.809 --> 00:02:53.366
Of course, please tell me.

60
00:02:53.646 --> 00:02:59.470
Over the last two weeks, Aarav has said that some older boys are teasing him on the school bus.

61
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:01.222
I'm sorry to hear that.

62
00:03:01.502 --> 00:03:02.953
Did he tell you their names?

63
00:03:04.303 --> 00:03:05.903
The conversation continues.

64
00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:08.465
He mentioned two boys from Class 6.

65
00:03:08.745 --> 00:03:11.796
He's become quiet and doesn't want to take the bus.

66
00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:13.569
Thank you for telling us.

67
00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:17.476
I'll speak to the transport in-charge and the Class 6 teacher today.

68
00:03:17.756 --> 00:03:19.335
I appreciate that.

69
00:03:19.615 --> 00:03:22.068
Could you let me know what action is taken?

70
00:03:22.348 --> 00:03:24.140
Yes, I'll call you by Friday.

71
00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.090
The conversation continues.

72
00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.309
Thank you.

73
00:03:28.589 --> 00:03:30.487
We just want him to feel safe.

74
00:03:31.837 --> 00:03:32.797
Part 5.

75
00:03:33.077 --> 00:03:34.123
Speak today.

76
00:03:35.373 --> 00:03:39.191
Prepare 3 questions for your next PTM (or for a friend's).

77
00:03:39.471 --> 00:03:43.290
Practise raising a concern: facts, then impact, then request.

78
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.176
That's the end of this lesson.

79
00:03:46.456 --> 00:03:51.107
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

80
00:03:51.387 --> 00:03:57.509
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

